This error message typically occurs when you are trying to access a member (variable, method, etc.) of an object that has not been initialized or instantiated. 

In other words, you are trying to use an object that has not been created yet or is set to null. To resolve this issue, you need to make sure that you are properly initializing the object before using it.

Here's an example to illustrate the error and its solution in C#:

```csharp
// Example class
public class MyClass
{
    public void MyMethod()
    {
        Console.WriteLine("Hello, World!");
    }
}

// Main program
public static void Main(string[] args)
{
    MyClass myObject; // Object reference, not instantiated yet

    myObject.MyMethod(); // Error: object reference not set to an instance of an object

    // Solution: Instantiate the object
    myObject = new MyClass();
    myObject.MyMethod(); // Now it works: Hello, World!
}
```

In this example, initially, `myObject` is declared but not instantiated. Hence, when trying to access `myObject.MyMethod()`, it throws the "Object reference not set to an instance of an object" error. After instantiating `myObject` with `new MyClass()`, it can be used without any errors.

Remember to always ensure you initialize objects correctly before using them to avoid this error.

实现给pdf加图片水印并下载的C#代码如下：

```csharp
using System;
using System.Drawing;
using System.Drawing.Imaging;
using System.IO;
using System.Text;
using System.Threading.Tasks;
using iTextSharp.text;
using iTextSharp.text.pdf;

public class PdfUtils
{
    public static void AddImageWatermark(string inputFilePath, string outputFilePath, string watermarkImagePath)
    {
        using (Stream inputPdfStream = new FileStream(inputFilePath, FileMode.Open, FileAccess.Read, FileShare.Read))
        using (MemoryStream outputPdfStream = new MemoryStream())
        {
            byte[] watermarkBytes = File.ReadAllBytes(watermarkImagePath);
            Image watermarkImage = Image.FromStream(new MemoryStream(watermarkBytes));

            PdfReader reader = new PdfReader(inputPdfStream);
            int pageCount = reader.NumberOfPages;

            using (PdfStamper stamper = new PdfStamper(reader, outputPdfStream))
            {
                for (int i = 1; i <= pageCount; i++)
                {
                    Rectangle pageSize = reader.GetPageSizeWithRotation(i);
                    PdfContentByte pdfContentByte = stamper.GetUnderContent(i);

                    float x = (pageSize.Left + pageSize.Right - watermarkImage.Width) / 2;
                    float y = (pageSize.Bottom + pageSize.Top - watermarkImage.Height) / 2;

                    pdfContentByte.AddImage(watermarkImage, watermarkImage.Width, 0, 0, watermarkImage.Height, x, y);
                }
            }

            File.WriteAllBytes(outputFilePath, outputPdfStream.ToArray());
        }
    }

    public static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        string inputFilePath = "input.pdf";
        string outputFilePath = "output.pdf";
        string watermarkImagePath = "watermark.png";

        AddImageWatermark(inputFilePath, outputFilePath, watermarkImagePath);
        Console.WriteLine("Watermark added successfully!");

        Console.WriteLine("Press any key to exit...");
        Console.ReadKey();
    }
}
```

