To implement a function similar to `div_u64()` from asm/div64.h in FreeRTOS, you can utilize existing data types and arithmetic operations provided by the language you are using (e.g., C) to perform the division on large numbers. Here's an example implementation:

```c
#include <stdint.h>

uint64_t div_u64(uint64_t dividend, uint32_t divisor)
{
    uint64_t quotient = 0;
    uint64_t remainder = 0;

    for (int i = 63; i >= 0; i--)
    {
        remainder <<= 1;
        remainder |= (dividend >> i) & 1;

        if (remainder >= divisor)
        {
            remainder -= divisor;
            quotient |= 1ULL << i;
        }
    }

    return quotient;
}
