Here is an example of how you can configure the filters and routing in Spring Cloud Gateway:

```java
import org.springframework.cloud.gateway.filter.GatewayFilter;
import org.springframework.cloud.gateway.filter.factory.RequestHeaderToRequestUriGatewayFilterFactory;
import org.springframework.cloud.gateway.filter.factory.RewritePathGatewayFilterFactory;
import org.springframework.cloud.gateway.route.RouteLocator;
import org.springframework.cloud.gateway.route.builder.RouteLocatorBuilder;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Bean;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Configuration;

@Configuration
public class GatewayConfig {

    private final SoapService soapService;

    public GatewayConfig(SoapService soapService) {
        this.soapService = soapService;
    }

    @Bean
    public RouteLocator customRouteLocator(RouteLocatorBuilder builder) {
        return builder.routes()
                // Define your REST endpoints and routes
                .route("rest_route", r -> r.path("/api/rest/**")
                        .filters(f -> f.filters(soapGatewayFilterFactory()))
                        .uri("http://rest_service_url")
                )
                .build();
    }

    @Bean
    public GatewayFilterFactory<SoapGatewayFilter> soapGatewayFilterFactory() {
        return new GatewayFilterFactory<SoapGatewayFilter>() {
            @Override
            public GatewayFilter apply(SoapGatewayFilter filter) {
                return filter;
            }
        };
    }

    @Bean
    public SoapGatewayFilter soapGatewayFilter() {
        return new SoapGatewayFilter(soapService);
    }

    @Bean
    public RequestHeaderToRequestUriGatewayFilterFactory requestHeaderToRequestUriGatewayFilterFactory() {
        return new RequestHeaderToRequestUriGatewayFilterFactory();
    }

    @Bean
    public RewritePathGatewayFilterFactory rewritePathGatewayFilterFactory() {
        return new RewritePathGatewayFilterFactory();
    }
}
```

In the above code, we define the `customRouteLocator` bean using `RouteLocatorBuilder` to create routes for REST endpoints. We apply the `soapGatewayFilterFactory` as a filter to the route using the `filters()` method.

You can define more routes with different REST endpoints and apply the necessary filters as needed. The `uri()` method specifies the backend REST service URL that you want to route the request to.

Note that you may need to configure additional filters or adjust the routing logic based on your specific requirements.

