In C++, you can use the `getline` or `split` function to split a string into parts based on a delimiter. Here's an example using the `getline` function:

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <string>
#include <sstream>
#include <vector>

int main() {
    std::string str = "Hello, how are you?";
    std::vector<std::string> parts;
    std::stringstream ss(str);
    std::string part;

    while (std::getline(ss, part, ' ')) {
        parts.push_back(part);
    }

    for (const auto& part : parts) {
        std::cout << part << std::endl;
    }

    return 0;
}
```

In this example, the `getline` function is used to split the string `str` into parts based on the space (' ') delimiter. Each part is then stored in the `parts` vector. Finally, the parts are printed one by one.

