Sure! Here's an example of C# code to smooth an array of points into a curved line using Bezier segments.

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;

public class Point
{
    public double X { get; set; }
    public double Y { get; set; }

    public Point(double x, double y)
    {
        X = x;
        Y = y;
    }
}

public class BezierCurve
{
    public static List<Point> SmoothPoints(List<Point> points, double smoothness)
    {
        List<Point> smoothedPoints = new List<Point>();

        for (int i = 0; i < points.Count - 1; i++)
        {
            Point currentPoint = points[i];
            Point nextPoint = points[i + 1];

            double controlPointX = (currentPoint.X + nextPoint.X) / 2;
            double controlPointY = (currentPoint.Y + nextPoint.Y) / 2;

            double controlPoint1X = currentPoint.X + (controlPointX - currentPoint.X) * smoothness;
            double controlPoint1Y = currentPoint.Y + (controlPointY - currentPoint.Y) * smoothness;

            double controlPoint2X = nextPoint.X - (nextPoint.X - controlPointX) * smoothness;
            double controlPoint2Y = nextPoint.Y - (nextPoint.Y - controlPointY) * smoothness;

            for (double t = 0; t <= 1; t += 0.1)
            {
                double x = Math.Pow(1 - t, 3) * currentPoint.X + 3 * Math.Pow(1 - t, 2) * t * controlPoint1X + 3 * (1 - t) * Math.Pow(t, 2) * controlPoint2X + Math.Pow(t, 3) * nextPoint.X;
                double y = Math.Pow(1 - t, 3) * currentPoint.Y + 3 * Math.Pow(1 - t, 2) * t * controlPoint1Y + 3 * (1 - t) * Math.Pow(t, 2) * controlPoint2Y + Math.Pow(t, 3) * nextPoint.Y;

                smoothedPoints.Add(new Point(x, y));
            }
        }

        return smoothedPoints;
    }
}

public class Program
{
    public static void Main()
    {
        List<Point> points = new List<Point>();
        points.Add(new Point(0, 0));
        points.Add(new Point(2, 4));
        points.Add(new Point(4, 1));
        points.Add(new Point(6, 6));
        points.Add(new Point(8, 2));

        double smoothness = 0.2;

        List<Point> smoothedPoints = BezierCurve.SmoothPoints(points, smoothness);

        foreach (Point point in smoothedPoints)
        {
            Console.WriteLine($"Smoothed Point: ({point.X}, {point.Y})");
        }
    }
}
```

In this code, we have a `Point` class to represent the points with `X` and `Y` coordinates. The `BezierCurve` class provides a static method `SmoothPoints` that takes an array of points and a smoothness parameter. It calculates the control points and adds the intermediate points of the Bezier curve to the `smoothedPoints` list.

In the `Main` method, we create an example array of points, define the smoothness factor, and call the `SmoothPoints` method to get the smoothed points. Finally, we print the smoothed points to the console.

