<textarea id="myTextarea" maxlength="255"></textarea>
```

JavaScript:
```javascript
const textarea = document.getElementById("myTextarea");

textarea.addEventListener("input", () => {
  const inputValue = textarea.value;

  if (inputValue.length > 255) {
    textarea.value = inputValue.slice(0, 255); // Trim the extra characters
  }
});
```

In the example above, the `maxlength` attribute on the textarea element sets the maximum length to 255 characters. The JavaScript code adds an event listener to the textarea's "input" event. When the user types or pastes something into the textarea, the event listener triggers and checks the length of the input value. If it exceeds the limit, it trims the string to the first 255 characters. This way, the user cannot input more than 255 characters into the textarea.

