- Remove the `use Illuminate\Foundation\Auth\User as Authenticatable;` line.
- Remove the `use Illuminate\Notifications\Notifiable;` line.
- Update the class definition to implement the `Illuminate\Contracts\Auth\Authenticatable` interface:
  ```php
  <?php

  namespace App;

  use Illuminate\Contracts\Auth\Authenticatable;
  use Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Model;

  class User extends Model implements Authenticatable
  {
      //
  }
  ```
- Update the `username` property of the `User` model to match the column name in your database. For example, if your username column is called `username`, update the model as follows:
  ```php
  protected $primaryKey = 'username';
  protected $keyType = 'string';
  public $incrementing = false;
  protected $fillable = [
      'username',
      'password',
  ];
