```

Step 3: Create the migration for the transactions table.

```
php artisan make:migration create_transactions_table --table=transactions
```

This will create a new migration file in the `database/migrations` directory.

Step 4: Open the created migration file and define the table structure.

```php
use Illuminate\Database\Migrations\Migration;
use Illuminate\Database\Schema\Blueprint;
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Schema;

class CreateTransactionsTable extends Migration
{
    public function up()
    {
        Schema::create('transactions', function (Blueprint $table) {
            $table->id();
            $table->string('description');
            $table->float('amount');
            $table->enum('type', ['credit', 'debit']);
            $table->timestamps();
        });
    }

    public function down()
    {
        Schema::dropIfExists('transactions');
    }
}
```

Step 5: Run the migration command to create the transactions table in the database.

```
php artisan migrate
```

Step 6: Create a seeder for generating sample data.

