    return 0;
}
```

In the C++ code, we include the `<iostream>` header to use standard input/output functionality. The `std::cout` stream is used to output the "Hello, World!" message, and `std::endl` is used to end the line. Finally, `return 0;` is added to the `main` function as it is required in C++.

