            std::cout << cell << " ";
        }
        std::cout << std::endl;
    }

    return 0;
}
```

In this code, the `parseCSV` function takes a filename as input and returns a vector of vectors of strings (representing the parsed CSV data). It reads the file line by line, then splits each line by commas to obtain individual cells. Finally, it adds each row (vector of cells) to the `data` vector.

