To achieve a throttle opening animation when the up key is pressed to control a locomotive, you can use Unity's animation system. Here's an example C# code that demonstrates how to do this:

```csharp
using UnityEngine;

public class LocomotiveController : MonoBehaviour
{
    public float speed = 5f;
    public AnimationCurve throttleCurve;

    private Animator animator;
    private float currentThrottle = 0f;

    private void Start()
    {
        animator = GetComponent<Animator>();
    }

    private void Update()
    {
        float input = Input.GetAxis("Vertical");

        if (input > 0)
        {
            currentThrottle += input * speed * Time.deltaTime;
            currentThrottle = Mathf.Clamp01(currentThrottle);

            float throttleValue = throttleCurve.Evaluate(currentThrottle);
            animator.SetFloat("Throttle", throttleValue);
        }
        else
        {
            currentThrottle = 0f;
            animator.SetFloat("Throttle", 0f);
        }
    }
}
```

In this code, a locomotive game object is assumed to have an Animator component attached to it. Additionally, an AnimationCurve is used to control the throttle opening animation. You can customize the `speed` and `throttleCurve` variables in the Inspector according to your preferences.

The `Start` method gets a reference to the Animator component for the locomotive. The `Update` method checks for the up arrow key being pressed (a positive input value). When the up key is pressed, the current throttle value is incremented based on the input, clamped to a range of 0 to 1, and the throttle curve is evaluated to determine the throttle animation value. This throttle value is then set to the "Throttle" parameter of the Animator.

When the up key is released, the current throttle value is reset to 0, and the "Throttle" parameter is set to 0 to close the throttle animation.

Make sure to set up your locomotive model and Animator controller to properly handle the "Throttle" parameter and the corresponding animation states.

