2. Use `LaunchedEffect` to perform an async operation (e.g., fetching data) and update the `resultState` with the obtained result:
```kotlin
LaunchedEffect(Unit) {
    val result = fetchData() // Replace with your async operation

    // Update state only if the result is not null
    if (result != null) {
        resultState.value = result
    }
}
```

3. In your composable, check the `resultState` and display the text only when the result is not null:
```kotlin
if (resultState.value != null) {
    Text(text = resultState.value!!)
} else {
