However, if you want to create a custom method to clamp a value between a range and map it to a different range, you can do it manually:

```csharp
public static float MapClamp(float value, float originalMin, float originalMax, float newMin, float newMax)
{
    return Mathf.Clamp((value - originalMin) / (originalMax - originalMin), 0f, 1f) * (newMax - newMin) + newMin;
}

float result = MapClamp(32f, 32f, 32f, 1f, 0.77f);
```

In this example, you are mapping the value 32 from the range [32, 32] to the range [1f, 0.77f]. Since the original range and the new range are the same, the result will always be the new minimum value, which is 0.77f.

