Qt exec() and exec_() are both event loop functions that start the event loop of a Qt application. They are typically used in the main() function of a Qt program to start the application and handle events.

The exec() function is the older form of starting the event loop and is available in older versions of Qt. It is typically used without arguments:

```cpp
int main(int argc, char *argv[]) {
    QApplication app(argc, argv);

    // ...

    return app.exec();
}
```

The newer form, exec_() (with an underscore), was introduced in Qt 4 to avoid conflicts with the exec() function provided by some operating systems. It is typically used as a member function of the QApplication class:

```cpp
int main(int argc, char *argv[]) {
    QApplication app(argc, argv);

    // ...

    return app.exec_();
}
```

Both functions start the event loop of the application, allowing it to process system events such as user input, timer events, network events, etc. The application will continue to run until the event loop is interrupted, either by a call to QApplication::quit() or when the main window is closed.

In most cases, you can use either exec() or exec_() interchangeably, as they have the same functionality. However, it is a good practice to use the newer form, exec_(), to avoid any potential conflicts with operating system functions.

Qt的exec()和exec_()是用于启动Qt应用程序的事件循环函数。它们通常在Qt程序的main()函数中使用，用于启动应用程序并处理事件。

exec()是较早的形式，可用于较早版本的Qt中。它通常在不带参数的情况下使用，如下所示：

```cpp
int main(int argc, char *argv[]) {
    QApplication app(argc, argv);

    // ...

    return app.exec();
}
```

exec_()是新形式，从Qt 4开始引入，以避免与某些操作系统提供的exec()函数冲突。它通常作为QApplication类的成员函数使用，如下所示：

```cpp
int main(int argc, char *argv[]) {
    QApplication app(argc, argv);

    // ...

    return app.exec_();
}
```

这两个函数都会启动应用程序的事件循环，允许它处理系统事件，如用户输入、定时器事件、网络事件等。应用程序将继续运行，直到事件循环被中断，要么通过调用QApplication::quit()函数，要么当主窗口关闭时。

在大多数情况下，你可以互换使用exec()和exec_()，因为它们具有相同的功能。然而，为避免与操作系统函数产生冲突，最好使用较新的形式exec_()。

