You can achieve this by keeping a count of columns within each row and closing the row when the count exceeds 4. Here's an example code in PHP:

```php
<?php
// Example array of columns
$columns = array('Column 1', 'Column 2', 'Column 3', 'Column 4', 'Column 5', 'Column 6', 'Column 7', 'Column 8', 'Column 9', 'Column 10');

// Check if there are any columns
if (!empty($columns)) {
    // Initialize count
    $count = 0;

    // Start the row
    echo '<div class="row">';

    // Loop through each column
    foreach ($columns as $column) {
        // Check if count exceeds 4
        if ($count >= 4) {
            // Close the row
            echo '</div>';

            // Start a new row
            echo '<div class="row">';

            // Reset count
            $count = 0;
        }

        // Output the column
        echo '<div class="col">' . $column . '</div>';

        // Increment count
        $count++;
    }

    // Close the last row
    echo '</div>';
}
?>
```

In this example, we have an array of columns. We loop through each column and increment the count. If the count exceeds 4, we close the current row and start a new row. This way, the columns are automatically transferred to another row when the count exceeds 4.

