To remove any bias and ensure an unbiased random signed integer, the function performs a bitwise XOR operation with `INT_MIN` (most significant bit set to 1) and separately subtracts the least significant bit of the unsigned integer to account for cases where the unsigned integer is a power of 2. These operations help in achieving an accurate uniform distribution of random signed integers.

The main function illustrates how the `generateRandomSignedInt()` function can be used to generate a random signed integer.

