To optimize this function for CPU and memory usage, we can implement two improvements: 

1. Use binary search: Instead of iterating through the lines one by one, we can use a binary search algorithm to find the line at the given position. This will drastically reduce the number of comparisons needed and improve the time complexity from O(n) to O(log n), where n is the number of lines.

2. Lazy initialization of line array: Instead of initializing the lines array each time the function is called, we can lazily initialize it. We can keep a reference to the lines array and only initialize it when it is needed or when the text has been edited. This will save memory and improve performance in cases where the lines array is not needed.

