To see which class has created a certain thread, you can use the `Thread.currentThread().getStackTrace()` method in Java. This method returns an array of stack trace elements, and you can analyze the elements to determine the class that created the thread. Here's an example:

```java
public class MyClass {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Thread thread = new Thread(new MyRunnable());
        thread.start();
    }
}

class MyRunnable implements Runnable {
    @Override
    public void run() {
        StackTraceElement[] stackTrace = Thread.currentThread().getStackTrace();
        if (stackTrace.length > 0) {
            // The first element is the most recent method call, so usually it represents the class that created the thread
            String className = stackTrace[0].getClassName();
            System.out.println("Thread created by class: " + className);
        }
    }
}
```

In this example, the `MyClass` creates a new thread by instantiating `MyRunnable`, and inside the `run` method, the stack trace is obtained. The first element of the stack trace is retrieved, and its class name is printed to the console, representing the class that created the thread.

Note that the accuracy of this method depends on the JVM implementation and the optimization level, so it may not always provide the intended result.

