Integrating AngularJS code within a React component requires some additional steps due to the differences between AngularJS and React. Here's a step-by-step guide:

1. First, ensure you have AngularJS and React dependencies installed in your project:
   ```shell
   npm install angular react
   ```

2. In your React component, create a container element (e.g., a div) where you will render the AngularJS code:

   ```jsx
   import React, { useRef, useEffect } from 'react';

   const AngularJSComponentWrapper = () => {
     const angularRef = useRef(null);

     useEffect(() => {
       // Load AngularJS library dynamically
       const script = document.createElement('script');
       script.src = 'https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/angular.js/1.8.2/angular.min.js';
       script.async = true;
       document.body.appendChild(script);

       // Wait for AngularJS to load
       script.onload = () => {
         // Bootstrap AngularJS manually
         angular.bootstrap(angularRef.current, ['YourAngularJSApp']);
       };

       // Clean up AngularJS when React component unmounts
       return () => {
         document.body.removeChild(script);
         if (angularRef.current) {
           angularRef.current.innerHTML = '';
         }
       };
     }, []);

     return <div ref={angularRef} />;
   };

   export default AngularJSComponentWrapper;
   ```

3. Create an AngularJS module and component in a separate file (e.g., `angularComponent.js`):

   ```javascript
   angular.module('YourAngularJSApp', []).component('angularComponent', {
     template: '<h2>AngularJS Code</h2>',
   });
   ```

4. In your AngularJS application's entry file (e.g., `index.html`), include the compiled React component and mount it:

   ```html
   <!-- Include the React app's bundle -->
   <script src="/path/to/react-app-bundle.js"></script>

   <!-- Mount the React component embedding the AngularJS code -->
   <div id="react-app"></div>

   <script>
     // Mount the React component
     ReactDOM.render(<AngularJSComponentWrapper />, document.getElementById('react-app'));
   </script>
   ```

   Replace `/path/to/react-app-bundle.js` with the actual path to your React application build bundle.

5. Start your AngularJS project, and you should see both the React and AngularJS code rendering properly.

With these steps, you can integrate AngularJS code within a React component in your project.

