To determine the free memory in an STM32 microcontroller, you can use the heap and stack pointers. Here is a step-by-step process to achieve this:

1. Include the necessary header files:

```c
#include <stddef.h>
#include <stdint.h>
#include "stm32fxxx.h" // Replace "xxx" with your specific STM32 model
```

2. Create a function to calculate the remaining free memory:

```c
size_t getFreeMemory(void) {
  extern uint32_t __StackLimit;
  extern uint32_t __StackTop;
  extern uint32_t __HeapLimit;
  extern uint32_t __HeapTop;

  size_t stackSize = (size_t)(&__StackTop - &__StackLimit);
  size_t heapSize = (size_t)(&__HeapTop - &__HeapLimit);

  size_t freeMemory = stackSize + heapSize;
  return freeMemory;
}
```

3. Use the `getFreeMemory` function wherever you need to determine the remaining free memory:

```c
int main(void) {
  // Other code...

  size_t freeMemory = getFreeMemory();
  // Use the value of `freeMemory` as needed

  // Other code...
}
```

Note: The actual names of the stack and heap pointers may vary depending on the STM32 model and the specific linker script used. In the provided code, `__StackLimit` and `__HeapLimit` are used as the bottom pointers, while `__StackTop` and `__HeapTop` are used as the top pointers. Make sure to modify the code accordingly based on your specific setup and linker script configuration.

