```

2. Create a new PHP file named "process_avatar.php" to handle the form submission and avatar updating.

Example PHP code (process_avatar.php):

```php
<?php
session_start();
require_once '../../functions/helpers.php';
require_once '../../functions/pdo_connection.php';

if (!isset($_SESSION['user_id'])) {
  echo 'Unauthorized access';
  exit;
}

$user_id = $_SESSION['user_id'];

if (isset($_FILES['avatar'])) {
  $file = $_FILES['avatar'];
  $file_types = array('image/jpeg', 'image/png', 'image/svg+xml', 'image/webp');

  // Check if file type is allowed
  if (in_array($file['type'], $file_types)) {
    $file_extension = pathinfo($file['name'], PATHINFO_EXTENSION);
    $new_avatar_path = '/avatars/' . $_SESSION['username'] . '.' . $file_extension;

    // Move the uploaded file to the avatars directory
    move_uploaded_file($file['tmp_name'], $_SERVER['DOCUMENT_ROOT'] . $new_avatar_path);

    // Update the avatar column in the user_avatars table
    $stmt = $pdo->prepare("UPDATE user_avatars SET avatar = ? WHERE user_id = ?");
    $stmt->execute([$new_avatar_path, $user_id]);

    // Redirect to the settings page
    header('Location: /settings.php');
    exit;
  } else {
    echo 'Invalid file type. Allowed formats: jpg, jpeg, png, svg, webp';
    exit;
  }
}
```

3. In the "change avatar" form, update the "action" attribute to point to the "process_avatar.php" file.

```html
<form method="post" enctype="multipart/form-data" action="process_avatar.php">
```

4. Finally, update the "avatar" column in the "user_avatars" table to store the URL of the new avatar image.

```php
$stmt = $pdo->prepare("UPDATE user_avatars SET avatar = ? WHERE user_id = ?");
$stmt->execute([$new_avatar_path, $user_id]);
```

This implementation allows the user to select an image file and upload it as their new avatar. The image file is then moved to the "/avatars" directory and the file path is stored in the "avatar" column of the "user_avatars" table.

