1. Create a Windows Forms application in your preferred programming language (e.g., C#, VB.NET).

2. Design the form with a numericupdown control and a panel control for displaying the dynamic textboxes. The panel will act as a container for the textboxes. Also, add a VScrollBar control to the form.

3. Set the `AutoScroll` property of the panel to `true` to enable automatic scrolling.

