I apologize for the confusion, but SpaceEngine is not a software that can be directly implemented using Java code. SpaceEngine is a standalone program developed in C++ specifically for Windows, Linux, and macOS.

However, if you're interested in creating your own space simulation program with Java, you can use various graphics libraries and frameworks such as JavaFX or LWJGL (Lightweight Java Game Library) to build your application. These libraries provide tools and utilities for rendering 3D graphics and can help you create a virtual space environment.

Here is a simple example using JavaFX to display a basic 3D scene:

```java
import javafx.application.Application;
import javafx.scene.Group;
import javafx.scene.Scene;
import javafx.scene.paint.Color;
import javafx.scene.shape.Box;
import javafx.scene.transform.Rotate;
import javafx.stage.Stage;

public class SpaceSimulator extends Application {

    @Override
    public void start(Stage primaryStage) {
        // Create a 3D box to represent a celestial object
        Box celestialObject = new Box(50, 50, 50);
        celestialObject.setTranslateX(200);
        celestialObject.setTranslateY(200);
        celestialObject.setTranslateZ(200);

        // Create a group to hold the objects in the scene
        Group root = new Group();
        root.getChildren().add(celestialObject);

        // Create a scene with a white background
        Scene scene = new Scene(root, 800, 600, Color.WHITE);

        // Set up camera positioning and movement
        scene.setCamera(new PerspectiveCamera());
        rotateScene(scene);

        // Set up stage
        primaryStage.setTitle("Space Simulator");
        primaryStage.setScene(scene);
        primaryStage.show();
    }

    private void rotateScene(Scene scene) {
        // Rotate the scene continuously
        Rotate rotation = new Rotate(0, Rotate.Y_AXIS);
        scene.getRoot().getTransforms().add(rotation);
        Timeline timeline = new Timeline(
            new KeyFrame(Duration.seconds(0), new KeyValue(rotation.angleProperty(), 0)),
            new KeyFrame(Duration.seconds(20), new KeyValue(rotation.angleProperty(), 360))
        );
        timeline.setCycleCount(Timeline.INDEFINITE);
        timeline.play();
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        launch(args);
    }
}
