Unfortunately, MySQL does not natively support a `REVERSE` function like other database systems. However, you can achieve the reverse functionality using a `WHILE` loop in a stored procedure. Here's an example of how you can do it:

```sql
DELIMITER //

CREATE PROCEDURE reverse_string(
    IN input_string VARCHAR(255),
    OUT output_string VARCHAR(255)
)
BEGIN
    DECLARE string_length INT;
    DECLARE reversed_string VARCHAR(255);
    DECLARE i INT DEFAULT 1;

    SET string_length = LENGTH(input_string);

    WHILE i <= string_length DO
        SET reversed_string = CONCAT(SUBSTRING(input_string, i, 1), reversed_string);
        SET i = i + 1;
    END WHILE;

    SET output_string = reversed_string;
END //

DELIMITER ;

-- Usage example:
SET @name = 'nancy';
CALL reverse_string(@name, @reversed_name);
SELECT @name AS name, @reversed_name AS reversedname;
```

