// Templated function to be called with each type
template<typename T>
void processType()
{
    // code to process each type goes here
}

// Variadic template to collect all types generated by template instantiation
template<typename... Types>
struct TypeCollector
{
    // Templated function to call with each collected type
    template<typename Func>
    static void callWithEachType(Func func)
    {
        // Expanding the parameter pack and calling the templated function
        (func.template operator()<Types>(), ...);
    }
};

// Usage example
int main()
{
    // Collecting all types generated by instantiation of the template with int, float, and char
    TypeCollector<int, float, char>::callWithEachType(processType);

    return 0;
}
```

In the above example, `TypeCollector` is a variadic template that takes in a list of types (`Types...`) generated by the template instantiation. The `callWithEachType()` function inside `TypeCollector` takes a templated function (`Func`) and iterates over each type, calling the provided function with each type in succession.

In the `main()` function, we demonstrate the usage by collecting the types `int`, `float`, and `char` using `TypeCollector` and calling the `processType()` function with each collected type. You can modify the list of types in `TypeCollector` as per your requirements.

