To create an express chat application using Websockets, you can follow these steps:

1. Installation:
   - Install Node.js if you haven't already.
   - Create a new folder for your project.
   - Open the terminal and navigate to the project folder.
   - Run the following command to initialize a package.json file: `npm init -y`
   - Install the required dependencies using the command: `npm install express express-ws`

2. Setup express.js:
   - Create a file named `index.js` in your project folder.
   - Import express and express-ws modules at the top of `index.js`:
     ```javascript
     const express = require('express');
     const expressWs = require('express-ws');
     ```
   - Create an instance of express and express-ws:
     ```javascript
     const app = express();
     const appWs = expressWs(app);
     ```
   - Declare a route for the websocket connection:
     ```javascript
     app.ws('/chat', (ws, req) => {
       // websocket connection logic
     });
     ```
   - Start the server by listening on a specific port:
     ```javascript
     const port = process.env.PORT || 3000;
     app.listen(port, () => {
       console.log(`Server started on port ${port}`);
     });
     ```

3. Websocket connection handling:
   Inside the `app.ws` route, you can add the logic to handle the websocket connection:
   ```javascript
   app.ws('/chat', (ws, req) => {
     ws.on('message', (msg) => {
       // Handle incoming message
       appWs.getWss().clients.forEach((client) => {
         if (client.readyState === WebSocket.OPEN) {
           client.send(msg);
         }
       });
     });

     ws.on('close', () => {
       // Handle closed connection
     });

     // Send initial message to the client
     ws.send('Welcome to the chat!');
   });
   ```

4. Create a basic HTML structure:
   - Create a file named `index.html` in the project folder.
   - Add the following HTML structure to `index.html`:
     ```html
     <!DOCTYPE html>
     <html>
       <head>
         <title>Express Chat</title>
       </head>
       <body>
         <h1>Express Chat</h1>
