```java
import processing.core.*;

PImage canvas;
int canvasSize = 512;  // Size of the canvas

void setup() {
  size(canvasSize, canvasSize, P3D);
  canvas = createImage(canvasSize, canvasSize, RGB);
  generateArt();
}

void draw() {
  // Save the canvas as an image
  saveCanvas(canvas, "NFT_" + frameCount, "png");
  // Stop the script when done generating the single frame
  exit();
}

void generateArt() {
  canvas.loadPixels();
  for (int x = 0; x < canvas.width; x++) {
    for (int y = 0; y < canvas.height; y++) {
      // Generate a random color for each pixel
      int pixelColor = color(random(255), random(255), random(255));
      canvas.set(x, y, pixelColor);
    }
  }

  // Generate random spheres
  int numSpheres = 10;  // Number of spheres to generate
  for (int i = 0; i < numSpheres; i++) {
    int sphereX = int(random(canvas.width));
    int sphereY = int(random(canvas.height));
    int sphereSize = int(random(10, 100)); // Random sphere size between 10 and 100 pixels

    // Generate a random color for the sphere
    int sphereColor = color(random(255), random(255), random(255));

    // Draw the sphere
    drawSphere(sphereX, sphereY, sphereSize, sphereColor);
  }

  canvas.updatePixels();
}

void drawSphere(int x, int y, int size, color fillColor) {
  pushMatrix();
  translate(x, y);
  fill(fillColor);
  noStroke();
  sphere(size);
  popMatrix();
}
```

This Processing script generates a 512x512 image with random colors and places random spheres on the canvas. The script will generate a single frame and save it as a PNG image. Feel free to modify the `numSpheres` variable to control the number of spheres to be generated.

The `generateArt()` function generates random colors for each pixel of the canvas and then randomly creates spheres at different positions with random sizes and colors. The `drawSphere()` function is used to draw each sphere on the canvas.

Once you run this script, it will create a PNG image that you can use as an NFT with generative art featuring random colors and spheres.

