Here's a Node.js function that generates a Luhn valid card number, expiry date, and CVC based on a given BIN (Bank Identification Number):

```javascript
function generateCardDetails(bin) {
  // Generate a random 9-digit account number
  const accountNumber = Math.floor(Math.random() * 900000000) + 100000000;

  // Combine the BIN and account number to create the card number
  const cardNumber = bin + accountNumber;

  // Calculate the Luhn check digit
  const digits = cardNumber.split('');
  let sum = 0;
  let even = false;

  for (let i = digits.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
    let digit = parseInt(digits[i], 10);

    if (even) {
      digit *= 2;

      if (digit > 9) {
        digit -= 9;
      }
    }

    sum += digit;
    even = !even;
  }

  const checkDigit = (sum % 10 === 0) ? 0 : (10 - (sum % 10));
  const luhnValidCardNumber = cardNumber + checkDigit;

  // Generate random expiry date (between current year and 5 years in the future)
  const currentYear = new Date().getFullYear();
  const expiryYear = currentYear + Math.floor(Math.random() * 6);
  const expiryMonth = Math.floor(Math.random() * 12) + 1;

  // Generate a random 3-digit CVC
  const cvc = Math.floor(Math.random() * 900) + 100;

  return {
    cardNumber: luhnValidCardNumber,
    expiryDate: `${expiryMonth}/${expiryYear}`,
    cvc: cvc
  };
}

// Example usage
const binNumber = '123456'; // Replace with your desired BIN number
const cardDetails = generateCardDetails(binNumber);

console.log(cardDetails.cardNumber);
console.log(cardDetails.expiryDate);
console.log(cardDetails.cvc);
```

This function generates a random 9-digit account number, combines it with the given BIN number to create a card number. It then calculates the Luhn check digit and appends it to the card number to make it Luhn valid.

For the expiry date, it generates a random month and year within the range of the current year and 5 years in the future. Finally, it generates a random 3-digit CVC.

You can replace the `binNumber` variable with your desired BIN number when calling the function.

