In this approach, you no longer need a separate XML file (`Student.hbm.xml`) for mapping. Instead, you define the `Student` class as a plain Java class with its properties. The mapping is now done in the `hibernate.cfg.xml` file using the `<mapping class="Student"/>` element to reference your `Student` entity class.

Remember to update the database connection details in the `hibernate.cfg.xml` file according to your specific setup.

