                scanf("%d", & value);
                enqueue(value);
                break;
            case 2:
                printf("The deleted element is %d\n\n", dequeue());
                break;
            case 3:
                display();
                break;
            case 4:
                printf("Exiting...\n");
                break;
            default:
                printf("Invalid choice! Please enter a valid option.\n");
                break;
        }
    }
    return 0;
}
```

This code implements a queue using a linked list. The program will display a menu to the user with four options: enqueue, dequeue, display the queue, and exit. The user can enter the desired option, and the corresponding function will be called. The main function will loop until the user chooses to exit.

