To register a mesh during the construction of a class in UE4 using C++, you can follow these steps:

1. First, you need to declare a `UPROPERTY` macro to specify the mesh component in your header file (.h):

```cpp
UPROPERTY(VisibleDefaultsOnly, BlueprintReadOnly, Category = StaticMesh, meta = (AllowPrivateAccess = "true"))
class UStaticMeshComponent* MeshComponent;
```

2. In the constructor of your class, initialize the `MeshComponent` and set the static mesh to it. Call `SetStaticMesh` to set the desired mesh:

```cpp
AMyClass::AMyClass()
{
    // Create the mesh component
    MeshComponent = CreateDefaultSubobject<UStaticMeshComponent>(TEXT("MeshComponent"));

    // Set it as the root component
    RootComponent = MeshComponent;

    // Load the desired static mesh from a file (e.g., "StaticMesh'/Path/To/MyMesh.MyMesh'")
    static ConstructorHelpers::FObjectFinder<UStaticMesh> MeshAsset(TEXT("/Path/To/MyMesh.MyMesh"));
    if (MeshAsset.Succeeded())
    {
        // Set the static mesh
        MeshComponent->SetStaticMesh(MeshAsset.Object);
    }
}
```

Note: Make sure you replace "/Path/To/MyMesh.MyMesh" with the actual path to your mesh asset.

3. Finally, you can customize the properties of your mesh component (e.g., collision, material) and add any additional functionalities as needed.

That's it! The mesh will be registered during the construction of your class, and you can access it through the `MeshComponent` variable.

