To get all keys from inside the array in JS, you can use the `reduce()` and `Object.keys()` methods. Here's an example:

```javascript
var a = {'a': [{'b': 'b'}, {'c': 'b'}, {'d': 'b'}]};

var allKeys = a.a.reduce(function(result, obj) {
  var keys = Object.keys(obj);
  return result.concat(keys);
}, []);

console.log(allKeys);
```

Output:
```
