В этой версии мы создаем `Vector2` координаты для каждой цели, используя только X и Z координаты. При проверке расстояния мы также используем только X и Z координаты позиции бота. Однако, когда мы перемещаем бота к цели, мы сохраняем Y-координату позиции бота, чтобы сохранить правильную высоту.

To generate a 12 KHz PWM signal using an ESP32 chip, you need to configure the appropriate registers and timers within the ESP32's hardware PWM module. Here's an example C code snippet that demonstrates how to achieve this:

```c
#include <driver/ledc.h>

// Macro to define the frequency resolution
#define PWM_RESOLUTION 8

void app_main()
{
    // Configure the PWM module
    ledc_timer_config_t ledc_timer = {
        .duty_resolution = PWM_RESOLUTION,
        .freq_hz = 12000,           // Frequency of 12 KHz
        .speed_mode = LEDC_HIGH_SPEED_MODE,
        .timer_num = LEDC_TIMER_0
    };
    ledc_timer_config(&ledc_timer);

    // Configure the PWM channel
    ledc_channel_config_t ledc_channel = {
        .channel = LEDC_CHANNEL_0,
        .duty = 0,                          // Initial duty cycle
        .gpio_num = GPIO_NUM_25,            // Output GPIO pin
        .speed_mode = LEDC_HIGH_SPEED_MODE,
        .timer_sel = LEDC_TIMER_0
    };
    ledc_channel_config(&ledc_channel);

    // Start PWM signal generation
    ledc_set_duty(ledc_channel.speed_mode, ledc_channel.channel, 128);  // 50% duty cycle
    ledc_update_duty(ledc_channel.speed_mode, ledc_channel.channel);
}
```

Make sure you have the ESP32 IDF (IoT Development Framework) set up with the necessary libraries and headers. Adjust the `.gpio_num` value according to the output pin you want to use for the PWM signal. Additionally, you can change the duty cycle by modifying the `ledc_set_duty` line.

