To create a web server in C#, you can use the built-in `HttpListener` class in the .NET Framework. Here's a simple example:

1. Create a new console application in Visual Studio.
2. Add reference to `System.Net` namespace.
3. In the `Main` method of your program, create an instance of `HttpListener`.
4. Add prefixes to define the URLs on which your server should listen to.
5. Start the `HttpListener`.
6. Enter a loop to handle incoming requests.
7. Process the request and provide a response.

Here's an example code snippet:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Net;

namespace WebServerExample
{
    class Program
    {
        static void Main(string[] args)
        {
            // Create a new HttpListener instance
            HttpListener listener = new HttpListener();

            // Add prefixes to listen on specific URLs
            listener.Prefixes.Add("http://localhost:8080/");

            // Start the HttpListener
            listener.Start();
            Console.WriteLine("Server started...");

            // Enter a loop to handle incoming requests
            while (true)
            {
                // Get the next incoming request
                HttpListenerContext context = listener.GetContext();

                // Process the request and provide a response
                string responseText = "Hello, World!"; // Your response

                // Set the response content type
                context.Response.ContentType = "text/plain";

                // Write the response string to the response output stream
                var responseBuffer = System.Text.Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(responseText);
                context.Response.ContentLength64 = responseBuffer.Length;
                context.Response.OutputStream.Write(responseBuffer, 0, responseBuffer.Length);

                // Close the response stream
                context.Response.OutputStream.Close();
            }
        }
    }
}
```

Note: Running the application with default settings may require administrative privileges as the server needs to listen on a specific port. You can change the port number or prefix to avoid such issues.

