JavaScript (script.js):
```javascript
function performOperation() {
    var num1 = parseFloat(prompt("Enter first number:"));
    var operator = prompt("Enter operation: (sum, multi, subtract, division)");
    var num2 = parseFloat(prompt("Enter second number:"));
    var result;

    switch (operator) {
        case "sum":
            result = num1 + num2;
            break;
        case "multi":
            result = num1 * num2;
            break;
        case "subtract":
            result = num1 - num2;
            break;
        case "division":
            if (num2 !== 0) {
                result = num1 / num2;
            } else {
                result = "Cannot divide by zero";
            }
            break;
        default:
            result = "Invalid operator";
    }

    document.getElementById("result").innerHTML = "Result: " + result;
}
```

In this example, when the user clicks the "Perform Operation" button, a series of `prompt()` method calls are made to gather the user's inputs (first number, operation, second number). The JavaScript function then performs the specified operation on the two numbers and displays the result on the webpage.

